# Silent Auction Database Schema

**Source of truth:** `<root>/original-immutable/data/database.sql` (DDL only — no seed data).  
**Database name:** `silent_auction`

## Frozen schema constraint

The database schema is **read-only** for migrations. Do not run `CREATE`, `ALTER`, or `DROP` on existing tables. Read and write **data** only through the structure below.

## Local connection

Use these values for local dev so the correctness harness can restore seed data before tests:

| Setting  | Value            |
| -------- | ---------------- |
| Host     | `localhost`      |
| Port     | `3306`           |
| User     | `root`           |
| Password | `password` |
| Database | `silent_auction` |

## Naming conventions

- DDL uses **PascalCase** table and column names (`Donor`, `DonorID`).
- Legacy PHP queries use **lowercase** table names (`donor`, `item`, …). Column names stay PascalCase in both.
- Migrated code should target the PascalCase names as defined in the DDL. On Windows MySQL, table names are case-insensitive; on Linux, align `lower_case_table_names` or use exact casing.

## Tables

### Donor

| Column       | Type                   | Notes                      |
| ------------ | ---------------------- | -------------------------- |
| DonorID      | INT PK, AUTO_INCREMENT |                            |
| BusinessName | VARCHAR(75)            | nullable                   |
| ContactName  | VARCHAR(75)            |                            |
| ContactEmail | VARCHAR(200)           |                            |
| ContactTitle | VARCHAR(75)            | nullable                   |
| Address      | VARCHAR(75)            |                            |
| City         | VARCHAR(30)            |                            |
| State        | VARCHAR(2)             |                            |
| ZipCode      | VARCHAR(5)             |                            |
| TaxReceipt   | BOOLEAN                | `0` = not sent, `1` = sent |

### Bidder

| Column     | Type                   | Notes          |
| ---------- | ---------------------- | -------------- |
| BidderID   | INT PK, AUTO_INCREMENT |                |
| Name       | VARCHAR(75)            |                |
| Address    | VARCHAR(75)            |                |
| CellNumber | VARCHAR(10)            |                |
| HomeNumber | VARCHAR(10)            | nullable       |
| Email      | VARCHAR(200)           |                |
| Paid       | BOOLEAN                | payment status |

### Category

| Column      | Type                   | Notes |
| ----------- | ---------------------- | ----- |
| CategoryID  | INT PK, AUTO_INCREMENT |       |
| Description | VARCHAR(75)            |       |

### Lot

| Column        | Type                   | Notes                         |
| ------------- | ---------------------- | ----------------------------- |
| LotID         | INT PK, AUTO_INCREMENT |                               |
| Description   | VARCHAR(75)            |                               |
| CategoryID    | INT                    | → Category                    |
| WinningBid    | DECIMAL(10,2)          | nullable until auction closes |
| WinningBidder | INT                    | → Bidder; nullable            |
| Delivered     | BOOLEAN                | item delivered to winner      |
| Image         | VARCHAR(500)           | nullable                      |

### Item

| Column      | Type                   | Notes                                                  |
| ----------- | ---------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------ |
| ItemID      | INT PK, AUTO_INCREMENT |                                                        |
| Description | VARCHAR(75)            |                                                        |
| RetailValue | DECIMAL(10,2)          |                                                        |
| DonorID     | INT                    | → Donor                                                |
| LotID       | INT                    | → Lot; **NULL** = unassigned (awaiting lot assignment) |

### Bid _(optional)_

Only needed for live self-service bidding. Composite PK `(LotID, BidderID, BidTime)`.

| Column   | Type          | Notes      |
| -------- | ------------- | ---------- |
| LotID    | INT           | → Lot      |
| BidderID | INT           | → Bidder   |
| BidTime  | DATETIME      | part of PK |
| Bid      | DECIMAL(10,2) |            |

## Relationships

```
Donor 1──* Item *──0..1 Lot *──1 Category
                Lot *──0..1 Bidder (WinningBidder)
                Lot 1──* Bid *──1 Bidder
```

- Items with `LotID IS NULL` are unassigned (lot-assignment workflow).
- Donor delete is blocked when items reference the donor (app-level FK guard in legacy).
- `TaxReceipt` is set to `1` after tax receipt generation.
- `Bid` table may be unused by current in-scope features but exists in schema.
